{"ts": 1784364330.132786, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode (no EXIT). Price ran favorably from entry almost immediately, reaching a peak of roughly +270pts by t=40m and closing the window around +130pts, with several sharp pullbacks (e.g. +168->+27 around t=25-28m) that each recovered to new highs rather than breaking down. Nothing in the run ever traded meaningfully against entry, so the thesis was intact throughout -- the deep pullbacks were dips within a strong favorable trend, not reversals, so bailing would have knifed a good trade. Next time: watch for a pullback that goes NEGATIVE (not just gives back gains) or that fails to make a new high after several attempts -- that combination, not giveback percentage alone, would be the real wrong-direction tell.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 52}
